  "term": "convulsant",
  "definition": "A convulsant is a substance that acts on the brain stem or spinal cord to trigger tonic or clonic convulsions, often by reducing the nervous system’s normal inhibitory control. These substances were once used to stimulate breathing or counter barbiturate overdose, but are now mainly used in research.",
